Southwest source and receiving ownership MUST satisfy the following boundaries.

The production roster MUST preserve all sixteen original logical placement keys,
including Tree_PineLean_A and Tree_PineLean_B. Each model MUST construct only its own
completed source with an explicitly recorded original random stream position.
Do not execute siblings or read sibling exports to recover random state.
Production geometry MUST use factory-startup source planners and one independently
cached export per bounded primary (at most 32768 triangles). File assembly MUST
require the complete current roster and MUST NOT export or join geometry.
Every original polygon and ordered corner MUST retain its one owner, winding,
normal, all UV/color values and names, material identity and authored pivot/frame.
Spatial pieces MUST remain separate native assets and retain their parent's
placement, shadow/culling/fade policy and complete logical local bounds.
Southwest's original FBX emitted only render geometry, with complex-as-simple native
queries. Mesh.colliders contains authoring diagnostics, NOT exported UCX; do not turn
those boxes into new blocking hulls. Each child MUST validate its own current cooked
LOD0 surface, no simple/convex leftovers and no external collision proxy.
Query products MUST capture final actual render tessellation before any exports.
Ferry and other query consumers MUST read that explicit complete source surface
instead of a whole render export or a partial child subset.
Validate and physically save every current native child before one combined
retirement preflight for obsolete pieces and the exact sixteen former parents.
Foreign references MUST refuse the entire retirement before any deletion. Require
physical parent/sidecar absence before task success; missing membership MUST fail
without loading any old parent as a fallback.
